          "y": -0.359375,
          "width": 1036,
          "height": 10121.15625,
          "top": -0.359375,
          "right": 1364.5,
          "bottom": 10120.796875,
          "left": 328.5
        },
        "targetText": "Actual PBPS projected reflection rotation and exact pair energyFan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang, arXiv:2609.06905v1 Appendix B.3 (B.21), projected rotation and pair energy. ASTIS supplies the internal zero-mean completion from the actual reflected law and conditional expectation.arXiv:2609.06905v1;Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib · PBPS2609.06905v1 Appendix B3 B21 A2.Ex15.m2; independent source graph P12/P13/P14 actual projected rotation and pair energy; P16/P17 corrector change and P19 B4 consumers. Mean(g)=0 is an internal completion from actual reflection-law preservation and conditional-expectation integral preservation. · faithful paraphraseComplete source statement (Samplinglib restatement)Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, inc",
        "bodyVisibility": "visible",
        "bodyDisplay": "block",
        "closedLeanDetails": 14,
        "mathContainers": 10,
        "png_path": "E:\\Samplinglib\\.astis\\pbps-actual-rotation70\\visual70-cdp\\unit0-statement.png"
      },
      {
        "label": "unit0-proof-1",
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:50371/example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
        "scrollY": 158814,
        "bodyHeight": 458540,
        "targetRect": {
          "x": 328.5,
          "y": 0.359375,
          "width": 1036,
          "height": 255.921875,
          "top": 0.359375,
          "right": 1364.5,
          "bottom": 256.28125,
          "left": 328.5
        },
        "targetText": "1. Retain the same actual probability geometry and operatorsUnfold the literal proposition and apply the independently accepted original-input parent. Retain its actual law, conditional kernel, reflection, centered defect root, inverse, polar isometry and globally centered-observable decomposition. The complete macro and micro subspaces have their inherited Hilbert structures.HP0=ker⁡⟨qP,⋅⟩,H⊥=ker⁡P,Rf=f−Pf.Corresponding Lean step  unfold actual_projected_rotation_statement\n  classical\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.",
        "bodyVisibility": "visible",
        "bodyDisplay": "block",
        "closedLeanDetails": 1,
        "mathContainers": 1,
        "png_path": "E:\\Samplinglib\\.astis\\pbps-actual-rotation70\\visual70-cdp\\unit0-proof-1.png"
      },
      {
        "label": "unit0-proof-2",
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:50371/example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
        "scrollY": 159093,
        "bodyHeight": 458540,
        "targetRect": {
          "x": 328.5,
          "y": -0.109375,
          "width": 1036,
          "height": 275.796875,
          "top": -0.109375,
          "right": 1364.5,
          "bottom": 275.6875,
          "left": 328.5
        },
        "targetText": "2. Prove mean preservation from the actual lawThe current U acts almost everywhere by the actual reflection F. The independently compiled augmentation invariance gives F#J=J, so change of variables preserves the integral. Conditional expectation preserves the full integral as well. Since J is a probability law, every L2 observable is integrable, and subtraction of actual representatives is legitimate.F#J=J,∫UudJ=∫udJ,∫PudJ=∫udJ,L2(J)⊂L1(J).Corresponding Lean step  let D : Hperp →L[ℝ] Hperp := R ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L Hperp.subtypeL\n  have hD (h : Hperp) : (D h : Lp ℝ 2 J)=\n      U (h : Lp ℝ 2 J)-P (U (h : Lp ℝ 2 J)) := hDparent h\n  have hIntertwine : V0.adjoint ∘L D= -(A0 ∘L V0.adjoint) := hIntertwineParent\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hμ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure J := hJ\n",
        "bodyVisibility": "visible",
        "bodyDisplay": "block",
        "closedLeanDetails": 1,
        "mathContainers": 1,
        "png_path": "E:\\Samplinglib\\.astis\\pbps-actual-rotation70\\visual70-cdp\\unit0-proof-2.png"
      },
      {
        "label": "unit0-proof-3",
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:50371/example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
        "scrollY": 159391,
        "bodyHeight": 458540,
        "targetRect": {
          "x": 328.5,
          "y": 0.296875,
          "width": 1036,
          "height": 225.46875,
          "top": 0.296875,
          "right": 1364.5,
          "bottom": 225.765625,
          "left": 328.5
        },
        "targetText": "3. Identify actual macro and micro compressionsInclude the centered macro space into the joint L2 space by iota. Orthogonality to ker P follows from selfadjointness of P. The same A0 and B0 split the reflected macro vector. The actual residual and polar-adjoint identities then identify its micro component without any range or surjectivity premise.PUιu=ιA0u,Uιu=ιA0u+i⊥B0u,RUιu=B0u,V0∗B0u=Γ0u.Corresponding Lean step  let ι : HP0 →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J := HP.subtypeL ∘L HP0.subtypeL\n  have hPι (u : HP0) : P (ι u)=ι u := hPf (u : HP)\n  have hOrth (u : HP0) (h : Hperp) : inner ℝ (ι u) (h : Lp ℝ 2 J)=0 := by\n    calc\n      inner ℝ (ι u) (h : Lp ℝ 2 J)=inner ℝ (P (ι u)) (h : Lp ℝ 2 J) := by rw [hPι]\n      _ = inner ℝ (ι u) (P (h : Lp ℝ 2 J)) := hPself.isSymmetric _ _\n      _ = 0 := by rw [show P (h : Lp ",
        "bodyVisibility": "visible",
        "bodyDisplay": "block",
        "closedLeanDetails": 1,
        "mathContainers": 1,
        "png_path": "E:\\Samplinglib\\.astis\\pbps-actual-rotation70\\visual70-cdp\\unit0-proof-3.png"
      },
      {
        "label": "unit0-proof-4",
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:50371/example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
        "scrollY": 159639,
        "bodyHeight": 458540,
        "targetRect": {
          "x": 328.5,
          "y": 0.375,
          "width": 1036,
          "height": 227.421875,
          "top": 0.375,
          "right": 1364.5,
          "bottom": 227.796875,
          "left": 328.5
        },
        "targetText": "4. Obtain the scalar energy and cross-term identitiesPositivity makes Gamma0 selfadjoint; A0 is selfadjoint already. Test A0^2+Gamma0^2=I against u to get the scalar norm identity. Move A0 and Gamma0 across the inner products and use their commutation to identify the two mixed terms.‖A0u‖2+‖Γ0u‖2=‖u‖2,⟨A0u,Γ0v⟩=⟨Γ0u,A0v⟩.Corresponding Lean step  have hΓself : IsSelfAdjoint ΓP0 := (show ΓP0.IsPositive from hPos0).isSelfAdjoint\n  have hEnergy (u : HP0) : ‖A0 u‖^2+‖ΓP0 u‖^2=‖u‖^2 := by\n    have h := congrArg (fun L : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => inner ℝ (L u) u) hSquare0\n    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.add_apply,ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply,\n      ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply,inner_add_left] at h\n    have ha : inner ℝ (A0 (A0 u)) u=‖A0 u‖^2 :=\n      (hA0self.isSymmetric (A0 u) u).trans (real_inner_s",
        "bodyVisibility": "visible",
        "bodyDisplay": "block",
        "closedLeanDetails": 1,
        "mathContainers": 1,
        "png_path": "E:\\Samplinglib\\.astis\\pbps-actual-rotation70\\visual70-cdp\\unit0-proof-4.png"
