        "targetText": "6. Derive the actual macro rotation by inner-product separationFor every centered macro test vector u, move P and U across the inner product using selfadjointness. Split U iota u into its actual macro/micro components; the cross-subspace terms vanish by orthogonality. The adjoint relation B0* fperp=Gamma0 fV and selfadjoint A0 identify the remaining terms. Separation identifies the already produced gP.⟨u,gP⟩=⟨Uιu,ιfP−i⊥f⊥⟩=⟨A0u,fP⟩−⟨B0u,f⊥⟩=⟨u,A0fP−Γ0fV⟩.Corresponding Lean step    have hgPformula : gP=A0 fP-ΓP0 fV := by\n      apply ext_inner_left ℝ\n      intro u\n      calc\n        inner ℝ u gP=inner ℝ (ι u) (ι gP) := rfl\n        _ = inner ℝ (ι u) (P g) := by rw [hPgp]\n        _ = inner ℝ (P (ι u)) g := (hPself.isSymmetric _ _).symm\n        _ = inner ℝ (ι u) g := by rw [hPι]\n        _ = inn",
