        "targetText": "8. Cancel mixed terms and retain every original witnessExpand the squared norms of the two formulas. The opposite mixed terms cancel by the cross-term identity, and the two scalar energy identities reduce the remaining sum to the input pair energy. Reassemble the complete original proposition with the same twelve witnesses. This is the projected rotation ingredient consumed by the subsequent actual B21 corrector change, not the remaining dynamics or main sampling theorem.‖A0fP−Γ0fV‖2+‖Γ0fP+A0fV‖2=‖A0fP‖2+‖Γ0fP‖2+‖A0fV‖2+‖Γ0fV‖2=‖fP‖2+‖fV‖2.Corresponding Lean step    have hgEnergy : ‖gP‖^2+‖V0.adjoint (R g)‖^2=‖fP‖^2+‖fV‖^2 := by\n      rw [hgPformula,hgVformula,norm_sub_sq_real,norm_add_sq_real,hCross]\n      nlinarith only [hEnergy fP,hEnergy fV]\n    exact ⟨fP,hfP,hBf,hΓf,hBudget,hVBudget,h",
